WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For those who couldn't tell
from the clip,

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:03.403 size:75% position:38% line:92%
you are three women.

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:05.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is --
You are committers of crimes.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:06.106 line:92%
-That's true. Yes, it is.

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:09.042 size:78% position:39%
We did commit a crime
in the pilot episode.

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:11.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
We will continue
to do bad things.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:12.779 line:92%
-Yeah. And it's really fun.

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:15.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a super funny show.
-Thanks.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:16.082 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-And a fantastic cast.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
You, Retta,
and Christina Hendricks.

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:20.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you immediately --
Did it become clear to you

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
were working with great people
right away?

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:23.757 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Oh, yeah. Right away.

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:25.959
I mean, the whole concept is
these women grew up together

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:30.096
and they all kind of get backed
into these financial situations

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:30.830 line:92%
that are really desperate.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.866
And it's kind of desperate times
call for desperate measures.

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:35.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I think one of the really
important elements is

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:36.169 size:81% position:41% line:92%
that we really believe

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they're all
really close friends.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:40.340
And so we actually ended up
having a producers' dinner

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.209
the first time we all three,
kind of, hung out together.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.478 size:84% position:42%
And it was very formal.
We had a nice cocktail.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.747
and then we sort of were like --
The producers went home

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:49.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we were like, "Mae, should
we have a nice dinner?"

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:54.254
Sure. So we went to dinner and
had about seven bottles of wine.

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:54.788 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:57.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then we were like, "Should we
keep having a nice time?"

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:59.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we went
to Christina's house.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:02.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
And all I know is somewhere
around the 3:00 mark I believe

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:05.765
I was like, "I'll be right back.
I'm gonna go to the restroom."

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:08.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Christina -- apparently,
I just never came back.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
And like an hour later --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:13.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like an hour later Christina
went looking for me

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:14.140 line:92%
and said her front door was ajar

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my pants were splayed out
on her dining room table.

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:19.479
And she, like, wandered into the
street and was like, "Mae?"

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:23.149
Like, with my pants thinking I
just wandered into the ocean

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:23.716 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
with no pants.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:26.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I just stole some of her
sweatpants and went home.

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:27.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:28.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Pretty classy stuff.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is classy.
-That's me, guys.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:32.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
-Invite me over.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:33.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That seems like
a real rookie move,

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:36.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you've been doing this
a long time.

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.297 line:92%
-I did it on purpose, okay?

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:38.465 line:92%
My character is irresponsible.

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:40.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was trying to
generate a relationship.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You were deep in character.
-That's right.

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:44.170 size:78% position:39%
I would never do that
in real life, Seth.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Of course.
-You know me. Come on.

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:46.573 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Well, you're very --

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, you have been doing this
since you were 3 years old.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's true, yeah.
-You've been in the business.

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:52.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you had parents
who were very --

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:54.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
wanted to make sure
you were ready for this.

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:55.548 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, Pat and Jeff.

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:57.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
They are extremely good
caretakers.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.586
They really wanted to prepare me
and actually

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:01.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
they may have prepared me
a little too much.

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:03.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a classic story that,
you know,

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.925
on a movie set everybody curses
like sailors.

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:07.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, it's the most intense
place to be.

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:10.697
-And so they said, "Okay, we're
gonna sit her down."

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:12.031 line:92%
And they said, "Now listen, Mae.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're gonna hear
a lot of words.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we want to tell you what
they are

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:17.837 size:88% position:44%
and we're gonna tell you
exactly what they mean,

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you must
never, ever use them."

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:21.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they, you know,
gave me the whole spiel.

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
The meanings, the words,
all of them.

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:26.312
And so apparently a couple days
later they got a call

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.147 line:92%
from my next door neighbor,

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:29.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
who I was best friends with
their kid at the time,

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:32.252
And the mom said, "Come on over
and see what's happening here."

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:35.488
And they peeked over the fence
and I was sitting in the pool,

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:37.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was going,
"Now, here are the words.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:41.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is what they mean but you
must never, ever use them."

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:41.661 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:44.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
To, like, this like 4-year-old
and her 2-year-old brother.

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:47.467
So yeah, you know, my best work.
-Very helpful.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:48.034 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Full disclosure.

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:50.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, Sarah Jessica Parker
was just here.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:50.970 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I know.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You are obsessed with her,
but kind of recently.

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:55.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Cool it. She's probably still
in the dressing room, Seth!

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:56.242 line:92%
-She probably still is, yeah.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, she's probably taking
your mug right now.

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:00.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, she probably is.
She can have it.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:02.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
She can have anything.
I've got a wallet.

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:03.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
Take the cash.
Whatever you need, SJP.

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:07.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But this is -- you --
"Sex and the City," this is --

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:10.490
-Yeah. I tend to come into
things a little too late.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:13.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
because whenever I start,
like, a new show or something,

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:14.661 line:92%
it really means a lot to me.

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:18.097
And I get so invested it's hard
for me to do anything else.

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:19.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I just started
"Sex and the City"

00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:21.968
like literally like a month ago.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:25.271
Retta was making so much fun of
me, 'cause I'd walk into set

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:29.142
and be like, "Oh, my God,
Carrie cheated on Aiden!

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:29.943 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Can you believe?"

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:32.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she was like,
"Yeah, 20 years ago.

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:35.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's pretty wild
to go through that."

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:37.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's really sad.
[ Applause ]

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.118 line:92%
I know. I'm trying. I'm trying.

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:42.055
-Do you just do it for
everything, not just that show?

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:44.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
Come in and be like,
"Lewinsky, have you heard?"

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:46.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Guys, it's crazy.
You don't understand.

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:50.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
I really -- the one other area
that I really struggled in

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:51.164 size:88% position:44% line:92%
is the "Hamilton" train.

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:54.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
It took me for freaking ever
to get on it.

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:56.336 size:75% position:38%
And Retta was, like,
so annoyed with me.

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:58.805
I mean, literally the only thing
I knew from "Hamilton"

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:00.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
was when the "Hamilton"
challenge came up,

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:03.409
Lauren Graham, who's still like
my best friend in the world.

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:04.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
We actually went hiking
in the mountains

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:07.947
and afterwards she was like,
"We're doing the challenge."

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:08.748 line:92%
And she taught me one song.

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:11.351
So that's, like, all I had to
relate to people at parties.

00:04:11.351 --> 00:04:13.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Oh, I know.
When she goes

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:14.120 line:92%
♪♪ a toast to the groom ♪♪

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
and like does the whole thing
I was like,

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:16.990 size:88% position:44%
Ah, that's crazy, right?
I've got to go though.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:17.657 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm gonna run out."

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
But Retta,
when she heard about this,

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:21.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
she totally flipped out
and she was like,

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:21.995 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"We're going this trip."

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:23.596 size:75% position:38%
So I went last night
for the first time!

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:25.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:25.265 --> 00:04:26.099 line:92%
-Thank you. It was so exciting.

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:28.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm always worried
that people who wait too long,

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:30.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
they'll hear
so much about "Hamilton"

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:31.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they will then
be underwhelmed.

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:34.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that does not seem like --
-I couldn't believe it.

00:04:34.007 --> 00:04:35.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
First of all, something really
humbling happened

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:38.344
when I was coming back in,
where I got there a little late

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.780
and I have, like, a really
nightmarish peeing problem

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:41.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
where it's like
every five minutes.

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:44.751
I'm like, "Well, now I have to
pee. I'm not enjoying the show."

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:47.353
So, like, I go like right
before the show starts.

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:48.087 line:92%
And when I came back in --

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:51.090
also the show "Good Girls" had
just premiered the night before.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:51.758 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And when I came back in,

00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:53.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
people kind of started to look
in my direction,

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they were like,
oh, kind of excited,

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:56.596 line:92%
taking out their cameras.

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:58.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"You guys, please.

00:04:58.364 --> 00:04:59.365 line:92%
It's really not a big deal."

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:00.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then literally
the three people

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:01.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
in front of me
turned around

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:04.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was, like, these three
beautiful blonde people.

00:05:04.404 --> 00:05:05.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was
the gold medal Olympians

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:07.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the cross country
skiing team.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:08.408 line:92%
And literally everybody's like,

00:05:08.408 --> 00:05:10.510
"Get out of the way, excuse me,"
like, pushing me aside.

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:13.379
And I was like, "Oh, okay, yes,
I mean, it's amazing."

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:14.047 size:88% position:44% line:92%
So that was pretty cool.

00:05:14.047 --> 00:05:15.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
And yeah, I mean,
my mind was blown.

00:05:15.448 --> 00:05:17.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's the most amazing thing
I've ever --

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:19.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I just want to point out
how kind Retta is

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:21.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
that she would take you
to that show

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:23.790
after you made this observation
on Instagram.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.926
You put a picture of Retta
next to a picture of The Rock

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:29.996
and you said, "When your costar
shows up to work

00:05:29.996 --> 00:05:30.997 size:84% position:42% line:92%
looking like The Rock."

00:05:30.997 --> 00:05:33.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I got to say
it's a pretty fair --

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:35.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, you guys.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:38.338
You guys -- it's the exact --
-It's the exact same outfit.

00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:40.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's literally
the exact same outfit.

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:41.574 line:92%
-You added the fanny pack.

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:44.377
-What do you mean?
That is a real fanny pack, Seth.

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:46.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would never
do something like that.

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:49.716
-Hey, congrats on the show.
It's always so great to see you.

00:05:49.716 --> 00:05:51.417 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Mae Whitman, everybody.

